Signed-off-by: Drew Macrae <drewmacrae@google.com>

  Every data structure in the .static_critical section should have the following:
    -A header file name.h that:
       -Defines the data type;
       -Has an extern declaration;
    -A source file <name>.c that:
       -Has a weak definition;
       -Related functions(optional);
    -A source file static_critical_name.c that:
       -Provides a definition of the data structure and places in the
        .static_critical.name section.

Signed-off-by: Douglas Reis <doreis@lowrisc.org>

- On page-load, create a tree of "wrap-W*" <div> nodes and "leaf-H*" <a>
  leaf-nodes that match the heirarchy of the section headings
  - e.g All headings after a <H1> (until the next <H1> or <H0>) can be
    thought-of as children of that node.
  - Leaf nodes are each navigation elements to their corresponding heading
    in the content body of the page.
  - Wrap nodes are styled with indentation to illustrate the heirarchy of
    the tree. This makes it easy to visually-parse the sections and
    subsections of the page.

- Add a :hover effect that changes all 'wrap' nodes that are parents of the
  currently-hovered leaf node. The effect changes the border-colourto be
  slightly darker.

//  /-> headerElements[idx] // In-order array of section headings down the page
//  |
//  |
//     // ----
//  0  // H1 |
//  1  // H1 |
//  2  // H1 |
//  -  // W1---------
//  3  // |      H2 |
//  4  // |      H2 |
//  -  // |      W2---------
//  5  // |      |      H3 |
//  6  // |      |      H3 |
//     // |      -----------
//  7  // |      H2 |
//  -  // |      W2---------
//  8  // |      |      H3 |
//     // ------------------
//  9  // H1 |
//  10 // H1 |
//  -  // W1---------
//  11 // |      H2 |
//  12 // |      H2 |
//  -  // |      W2---------
//  13 // |      |      H3 |
//  14 // |      |      H3 |
//     // |      -----------
//  15 // |      H2 |
//  -  // |      W2---------
//  16 // |      |      H3 |
//     // ------------------
//  17 // H1 |
//     // ----
//
//  LeafNode -> createAnchorElement(idx)

