The old Hugo documentation would set IDs for Markdown headings using {#id}
syntax. Mdbook will assign IDs automatically from the heading text.

Signed-off-by: James Wainwright <james.wainwright@lowrisc.org>

This commit adds a library to enable test binaries to query which boot
stage they are executing from. For example:

```c

...

if (kBootStage == kBootStageOwner) {
  // Do something specific if running the program from the first silicon
  // owner boot stage.
}
```

The execution environments have been updated to inject the correct
library based on their configuration.

